# Rally Supreme — Cursor Project Rules
# This file gives Cursor context about the project so suggestions are accurate.

## What this project is
Interactive exploded-view motorcycle parts fiche viewer.
Converts 2D fiche diagrams into interactive, clickable part assemblies.
Owner is building this for their own 1997 Honda XR650L (second gear failure).

## Tech stack
- Vite + vanilla JS (no framework)
- Three.js r160+ for sprite-based 3D viewer
- Python 3 for segmentation pipeline (segment_parts.py, sam2_segment.py)
- Node.js for validation scripts
- No database, no auth, no backend — pure static files + client JS

## Project structure
```
index.html                  ← Vite entry point
src/
  main.js                   ← reads ?slug= from URL, boots viewer
  viewer/
    RallyViewer.js          ← main viewer controller
    loaders.js              ← JSON + texture loading, returns {sprites, missing}
    scene.js                ← Three.js orthographic camera setup
    interaction.js          ← raycast click/hover, drag vs click detection
  ui/
    InfoPanel.js            ← slide-in part detail panel
    Controls.js             ← explode slider, BG toggle, missing assets
  styles/
    app.css
scripts/
  validate-assembly.js      ← Node validator, run: node scripts/validate-assembly.js <slug>
public/data/<slug>/
  assembly.json             ← assembly metadata
  parts.json                ← part records (what each part IS)
  placements.json           ← spatial data (where each part LIVES in diagram)
  diagram.png               ← source fiche image
  manifest.json             ← generated by build pipeline
  parts/
    001.png                 ← segmented part cutouts (RGBA, transparent bg)
    002.png
placement-tool.html         ← standalone authoring tool, no server needed
segment_parts.py            ← rembg-based segmentation pipeline
sam2_segment.py             ← SAM2 interactive click-to-segment tool
PIPELINE.md                 ← canonical data contract, READ THIS FIRST
```

## The canonical data contract
PIPELINE.md is the single source of truth. When in doubt, check it.
Key rules:
- All coordinates normalized 0.0–1.0 relative to diagram image dimensions
- Y-axis is FLIPPED: diagram top-left → Three.js center-up
- explode_vector[1] is negated in loaders.js (one place, documented)
- segment_image filename rule: label_to_filename(label) = parts/NNN.png (zero-padded to 3 digits)
- schema_version: 2 required in every assembly.json

## assembly.json schema (v2)
```json
{
  "schema_version": 2,
  "slug": "honda-xr650l-1997-carburetor",
  "brand": "Honda",
  "model": "XR650L",
  "year": 1997,
  "assembly": "CARBURETOR",
  "diagram_image": "diagram.png",
  "canvas": { "width": 1500, "height": 783 },
  "viewer_defaults": {
    "world_height": 10,
    "world_depth": 6,
    "explode_distance": 2.2,
    "show_background_diagram": true,
    "background_opacity": 0.22
  },
  "source": { "provider": "cmsnl", "url": "" }
}
```

## parts.json schema
```json
[{
  "label": "4",
  "part_number": "23431-MN9-000",
  "name": "GEAR, COUNTERSHAFT SECOND (28T)",
  "qty": "1",
  "notes": "Common failure point — inspect gear dogs for wear.",
  "superseded_by": "",
  "assembly_slug": "honda-xr650l-1997-transmission"
}]
```

## placements.json schema
```json
[{
  "label": "4",
  "x": 0.412, "y": 0.388, "z": 0.0,
  "depth_order": 60,
  "explode_vector": [0.4, 0.5, 0.0],
  "segment_image": "parts/004.png",
  "bbox": { "x": 0.36, "y": 0.35, "w": 0.11, "h": 0.09 },
  "anchor": { "x": 0.5, "y": 0.5 }
}]
```

## Explode vector conventions
- Above center:  [0,  1.5, 0]
- Below center:  [0, -1.2, 0]
- Left:          [-0.8, 0, 0]
- Right:         [0.8,  0, 0]
- Front (cover): [0, 0,  0.4]
- Rear:          [0, 0, -0.2]
- Fixed center:  [0, 0,  0]
Y-up = physically upward. Viewer negates Y internally.

## Depth order conventions
- Outer cover:    90
- Gasket:         80
- Pressure plate: 70
- Friction discs: 60
- Steel discs:    50
- Inner hub:      40
- Basket:         30
- Shaft/gear:     20
- Bearings:       10

## Key npm commands
```bash
npm run dev                                          # start viewer on localhost:5173
npm run validate:assembly -- <slug>                  # validate one assembly
node scripts/validate-assembly.js <slug>             # same thing
python3 segment_parts.py --slug <slug>               # rembg segmentation
python3 sam2_segment.py --assembly-dir public/data/<slug>/  # SAM2 interactive
```

## Current assemblies
