## Coding conventions
- ES modules throughout (type: module in package.json)
- No TypeScript — plain JS with JSDoc where helpful
- No framework — vanilla JS + Three.js only
- Errors should be loud and specific, never silent
- Fallback sprites (orange dashed box) for missing images — never skip rendering a part
- All coordinate math goes through worldMapper.toWorld() — never raw pixel math in viewer

## Things that have already been fixed — do not revert
- OrbitControls import: 'three/addons/controls/OrbitControls.js' (not examples/jsm)
- validate-assembly.js argv: filters '--' separator before reading slug
- background_opacity: read from assembly.json viewer_defaults, passed to Controls
- loadTextures returns {sprites, missing} not just sprites array

## What NOT to do
- Do not add Postgres, auth, user accounts
- Do not add TypeScript unless explicitly asked
- Do not use React or any framework
- Do not break the PIPELINE.md coordinate contract
- Do not construct file paths in the viewer — use segment_image verbatim from placements.json
- Do not add auto-hotspot detection — manual placement via placement-tool.html is correct
